# Services

---

# PartyKit Service

**`services/party`** - Real-time WebSocket Server

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────┐
│      PartyKit Server                   │
│                                         │
│  ┌──────────┐      ┌──────────┐       │
│  │  Server  │◄────►│ Clients  │       │
│  │(WebSocket)│      │(Browsers)│       │
│  └──────────┘      └──────────┘       │
│                                         │
│  Room-based broadcasting                │
│  (one room per course)                  │
└────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Each course = separate room for isolated presence

---

# PartyKit Implementation

**Server** (`src/server.ts`):
```typescript
export default class TutorsServer implements Party.Server {
  constructor(readonly room: Party.Room) {}

  onConnect(conn: Party.Connection) { /* Client joined */ }

  onMessage(message: string, sender: Party.Connection) {
    // Broadcast to all except sender
    this.room.broadcast(message, [sender.id]);
  }

  onClose(conn: Party.Connection) { /* Client left */ }
}
```

---

# PartyKit Client

```typescript
import PartySocket from "partysocket";

const socket = new PartySocket({
  host: PUBLIC_party_kit_main_room,
  room: courseId  // Room per course
});

socket.addEventListener("message", (event) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
  // Update presence UI
});

socket.send(JSON.stringify({
  type: "presence",
  user: userId,
  page: currentPage
}));
```

---

